*! cleanplots4vr v1.1.0 Trenton Mize 2026-10-12
*! Reversed ordinal companion scheme to cleanplots: 4 sequential viridis colors
*
* Same 4 palette colors as cleanplots4v, in exactly reverse order.
* Low categories are darkest; high categories are lightest (dark purple to light yellow).
* Retains the cleanplots legend, sizing, symbols, and line patterns.
*
* Color source: viridis (van der Walt & Smith 2015); sampled at end=.95, reversed.
* Matching R scale:
*   scale_color_viridis_d(option = "viridis", end = 0.95, direction = 1)
*   Note: matching endpoints require begin=.0; direction=1 produces a
*   dark-to-light scale, from darkest to end=.95 (rather than 1.0).
*   Use begin=0, end=.95 explicitly when comparing.
*
* Colors recycle after 4 plots; Stata has 15 plot slots.
* Bar and area color settings inherit the 70 percent intensity.
* Example: graph bar price, over(rep78) asyvars scheme(cleanplots4vr)

#include cleanplots


color p1              "68 1 84"
color p1line          "68 1 84"
color p1lineplot      "68 1 84"
color p1markline      "68 1 84"
color p1bar           "68 1 84"
color p1barline       "68 1 84"
color p1area          "68 1 84"
color p1arealine      "68 1 84"
color p1pie           "68 1 84"
linepattern p1line solid
linepattern p1lineplot solid
symbol p1 smcircle

color p2              "50 100 142"
color p2line          "50 100 142"
color p2lineplot      "50 100 142"
color p2markline      "50 100 142"
color p2bar           "50 100 142"
color p2barline       "50 100 142"
color p2area          "50 100 142"
color p2arealine      "50 100 142"
color p2pie           "50 100 142"
linepattern p2line dash
linepattern p2lineplot dash
symbol p2 smsquare

